    "summary": "Reports on social media that the U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control had lifted sanctions against Sheikh Hassan Dahir Aweys are false. OFAC merely merged 18 duplicate entries on July 27, 2026, leaving his designation intact.",
    "content": "The U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) has not removed sanctions against Sheikh Hassan Dahir Aweys, contrary to rumors circulating on Somali social media. An examination of official OFAC records shows no delisting action was taken.\n\nOn July 27, 2026, OFAC announced a technical consolidation of its sanctions database, merging 18 duplicate entries for various individuals and entities. Aweys's name appeared among these records, leading to the erroneous conclusion that sanctions had been lifted. However, the update was purely administrative and his designation remains in effect.\n\nSheikh Hassan Dahir Aweys is a prominent Somali figure who has been under U.S. sanctions since 2001 for his alleged ties to terrorist organizations. He was listed as a Specially Designated Global Terrorist. The OFAC decision last week only removed redundant records, not his sanctions status.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this distinction is important because misinformation about sanctions relief could affect financial transactions and international relations. Any actual removal of sanctions would require a formal delisting process, which has not occurred.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/29/maxaa-ka-jira-warka-sheegaya-in-cunaqabataynta-laga-qaaday-sheekh-xasan-daahir-aweys/",
